items.description:
Follow-up to #438. The guides cover the software search well but leave common situations unanswered:
- searching with no internship, or after graduating;
- advanced degrees, career switchers and location choices;
- Canada and India, although the board covers both;
- rotational programs, staffing agencies and contract roles;
- adjacent technical roles;
- cover letters, GPA cutoffs, career fairs and cold emails;
- portfolios and open source;
- OPT unemployment days, cap-exempt H-1B and other visas;
- rescinded offers, employment agreements and the first 90 days;
- how the board reads salary ranges.

The redesign mockup proposed 25 such guides. Four overlap existing guides (frontend, embedded and security interview prep are already in role-specific technical preparation; deadline extensions are in comparing offers), so this issue covers the other 21.

Also out of date: "What counts as a new grad job" says contract and staffing-agency roles are not excluded. That stopped being true when temporary, contract and fractional-FTE titles were excluded in #437. Three guides also link a USCIS H-1B page that no longer loads.

## Standard for each new guide
- Front matter per AGENTS.md: published, format, use_when / you_get. The brief may not state a number the body doesn't.
- 700–1,300 words; supported Markdown only.
- Every rule, number or quote links an official or primary source opened at writing time. No invented statistics.
- Claims about NGJ's own behaviour match the code.
- Field-neutral unless the topic is field-specific; no advice to misrepresent anything.
- Independently fact-checked before merge.

## Acceptance
- The 21 guides above, fact-checked.
- start-here and the reading paths updated together; the sync test passes.
- The "What counts" exclusions corrected and the USCIS link fixed.
- Content tests, build and a five-width browser sweep of every guide pass.
